{"4208640": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Dead Exposure", "steam_appid": 4208640, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>About This Game</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Dead Exposure is a short-form analog horror experience (1–1.5 hours) set inside a foreclosed home that won’t stay still.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You are sent to document the property after a family tragedy.  Armed with a Polaroid camera and a child’s toy modified to detect anomalies, you begin to notice things that shouldn’t exist.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Some only appear in photographs.<br>Others emerge when captured on film.<br>The act of observing changes what is there.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a slow-burn, liminal horror experience focused on tension, atmosphere, and uncovering what hides beneath the surface.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>The Experience</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>See beyond reality</strong><br>Your camera reveals objects and entities invisible to the naked eye.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A world altered by observation</strong><br>What appears on film doesn’t always match what is right in front of you.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Liminal, slow-burn horror</strong><br>Tension builds through subtle changes, absence, and unease.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Best experienced in one sitting</strong><br>A focused 1–1.5 hour experience designed to be played in the dark with headphones.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Features</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Reveal hidden realities using your camera</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Entities visible only through photographs</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Environmental storytelling through fragmented clues</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >EMF toy (“Clev